FPC 3.2.0 declares FpIOCtl's request argument as cInt on Linux, so the
$80086601 request for FS_IOC_GETFLAGS does not fit in a signed 32-bit
constant. FPC 3.2.2 changed TIOCtlRequest to culong, which is why upstream
requires 3.2.2. Keep the identical 32-bit bit pattern; the compiler
zero-extends it into the argument register, so ioctl receives the same value.

--- a/components/doublecmd/dclinux.pas
+++ b/components/doublecmd/dclinux.pas
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
   CLOSE_RANGE_CLOEXEC = (1 << 2);
 
 const
-  FS_IOC_GETFLAGS = $80086601;
+  FS_IOC_GETFLAGS = LongInt($80086601);
   FS_IOC_SETFLAGS = $40086602;
   (*
    * Inode flags (FS_IOC_GETFLAGS / FS_IOC_SETFLAGS)
